    <mj-text padding="20px 20px 10px 20px" font-family="Arial" color="#000000">
  <h3 style="font-size: 20px; line-height: 1.2; font-weight: 700; margin: 0;">Art &amp; culture</h3>
</mj-text>
<mj-table
  font-family="Arial"
  cellpadding="0"
  cellspacing="0"
  padding="0px 32px 0px 32px"
  style="width: 100%"
>
  <tr>
  <td style="
    font-size: 18px;
    vertical-align: top;
    line-height: 24px;
    padding-bottom: 15px;
    padding-right: 8px;
  "> &#8226; </td>
  <td style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 24px;
    padding-bottom: 15px;
    padding-left: 0px;
  ">
    <a href="https://www.timeout.com/london/news/londons-barbican-will-be-transformed-by-a-vast-immersive-exhibition-this-summer-030626" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #80011F; color: black;">The Barbican Centre in London will host a large immersive film and art exhibition titled <em>In Other Worlds</em> from May 21 to September 6, 2026</a>. The exhibition will explore imagined futures through science fiction, climate themes, and technological speculation. It will feature collaborations with artists, scientists, musicians, and designers linked to major productions such as Westworld, Fallout, The Handmaid’s Tale, and Andor.
  </td>
</tr>
<tr>
  <td style="
    font-size: 18px;
    vertical-align: top;
    line-height: 24px;
    padding-bottom: 15px;
    padding-right: 8px;
  "> &#8226; </td>
  <td style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 24px;
    padding-bottom: 15px;
    padding-left: 0px;
  ">
    <a href="https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/theatre-dance/news/timothee-chalamet-opera-ballet-disrespectful-b2933295.html" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #80011F; color: black;">Actor Timothée Chalamet has sparked backlash after saying “no one cares” about ballet or opera during a public conversation with Matthew McConaughey</a>. The remarks drew criticism from performers and industry figures in the classical arts, who said the comments dismissed centuries-old art forms and the artists who practice them. Opera singers, ballet professionals, and cultural leaders responded online, arguing that both disciplines remain vibrant and influential.
  </td>
</tr>
</mj-table>
<mj-text padding="20px 20px 10px 20px" font-family="Arial" color="#000000">
  <h3 style="font-size: 20px; line-height: 1.2; font-weight: 700; margin: 0;">Sports</h3>
</mj-text>
<mj-table
  font-family="Arial"
  cellpadding="0"
  cellspacing="0"
  padding="0px 32px 0px 32px"
  style="width: 100%"
>
  <tr>
  <td style="
    font-size: 18px;
    vertical-align: top;
    line-height: 24px;
    padding-bottom: 15px;
    padding-right: 8px;
  "> &#8226; </td>
  <td style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 24px;
    padding-bottom: 15px;
    padding-left: 0px;
  ">
    <a href="https://www.bbc.com/sport/formula1/articles/cn0zxv2vkj2o" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #80011F; color: black;">The Australian Grand Prix has announced that Turn Six at Melbourne’s Albert Park Circuit will be temporarily renamed “In Her Corner” for the 2026 race</a> to mark International Women’s Day. The tribute honours two prominent female Formula 1 engineers: Laura Mueller, race engineer at Haas for driver Esteban Ocon, and Hannah Schmitz, Red Bull’s head of race strategy. Organisers say the initiative aims to highlight women’s contributions to engineering and inspire more young people to pursue careers in the field.
  </td>
</tr>
<tr>
  <td style="
    font-size: 18px;
    vertical-align: top;
    line-height: 24px;
    padding-bottom: 15px;
    padding-right: 8px;
  "> &#8226; </td>
  <td style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 24px;
    padding-bottom: 15px;
    padding-left: 0px;
  ">
    <a href="https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/articles/c15xd7741zxo" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #80011F; color: black;">Leeds United has urged supporters to show respect when play is paused during Sunday’s FA Cup match against Norwich City</a>, allowing Muslim players observing Ramadan to break their fast. The appeal follows boos heard during a similar pause in last weekend’s game against Manchester City at Elland Road. The club condemned the reaction and acknowledged that some fans may not have understood why the match was briefly halted.
  </td>
</tr>
</mj-table>
